"L1, John 10:16: \"And other sheep I have, which are not of this fold: them also I must bring, and they shall hear my voice; and there shall be one fold, [and] one shepherd.\" John 10:27: \"My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me:\" The other sheep are already his (\"I have\"), and they shall hear his voice, the mark 10:27 gives of his sheep.\nL2, lexicon: \"other\" is allos (G243), \"else, i.e. different (in many applications)\"; it says other, not same kind (1 Corinthians 15:39 uses it of flesh of a different kind). The kind is carried by \"sheep\", probaton (G4263), \"something that walks forward (a quadruped), i.e. (specially), a sheep\", and the ownership by \"I have\", echo (G2192), \"to hold ... such as possession\". \"this fold\" is aule (G833), \"a yard ... court, (sheep-)fold, hall, palace\"; \"one fold\" is poimne (G4167), \"a flock ... fold\", a different word, and the KJV \"one fold\" renders poimne. \"must\" is dei (G1163), \"it is necessary (as binding)\". The \"one\" (G1520) of one flock and one shepherd is the same word as John 11:52's \"gather together in one\" (Conclusion 59).\nL3, cross-reference: Matthew 15:24, \"I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel\"; Ezekiel 34:12, \"so will I seek out my sheep, and will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day\" (margin: \"As...: Heb. According to the seeking\"); 34:23, \"I will set up one shepherd over them ... my servant David\"; 34:30-31, \"they, [even] the house of Israel, [are] my people ... ye my flock, the flock of my pasture, [are] men\"; Ezekiel 37:22, \"they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all\"; John 11:52, \"gather together in one the children of God that were scattered abroad\". On these the other sheep are read as the scattered house of Israel, and John 10:16 as the gathering of Ezekiel 34 and 37 under one shepherd. Held at L3 per DG-19, never stated as L1.\nL4: none. Scope: not a census proof; no per-person verdict (DG-1, DG-20); the Shepherd names the sheep (DG-12)."
